WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.933 --> 00:00:05.466
Continuing their journey to Cyllage City,

2
00:00:05.533 --> 00:00:08.666
where Ash's next Kalos Gym battle will take place,

3
00:00:08.733 --> 00:00:11.733
our heroes have just arrived in Camphrier Town.

4
00:00:15.366 --> 00:00:17.266
So this is Camphrier Town!

5
00:00:17.333 --> 00:00:20.366
The town map says it's a place is where you can taste the ages!

6
00:00:20.433 --> 00:00:22.533
What does taste the ages mean?

7
00:00:22.599 --> 00:00:24.666
It means the town has a wealth of history

8
00:00:24.733 --> 00:00:26.933
with a lot of old buildings still standing.

9
00:00:29.366 --> 00:00:31.966
- So loud!
- My ears!!

10
00:00:32.033 --> 00:00:33.699
What a terrible noise!

11
00:00:33.766 --> 00:00:35.833
Yeah. Wonder what it is!

12
00:00:37.433 --> 00:00:39.533
- Huh?
- That's weird. It stopped.

13
00:00:39.600 --> 00:00:41.433
- What a relief.
- Huh?

14
00:00:41.500 --> 00:00:46.633
Hi. Excuse me, but what was that awful sound just now?

15
00:00:46.699 --> 00:00:51.866
- Uh... Excuse me!
- Huh! I'm sorry. Just one second.

16
00:00:51.933 --> 00:00:55.933
Uh, I was wondering if you knew what that terrible noise was just now.

17
00:00:56.000 --> 00:00:59.366
Oh. That noise. Follow me.

18
00:01:00.599 --> 00:01:02.900
Huh?

19
00:01:02.966 --> 00:01:05.966
♪ I want to be the very best ♪

20
00:01:06.033 --> 00:01:09.399
♪ Like no one ever was ♪

21
00:01:09.466 --> 00:01:12.300
♪ To catch them is my real test ♪

22
00:01:12.366 --> 00:01:15.200
♪ To train them is my cause ♪

23
00:01:15.266 --> 00:01:18.399
♪ Pokémon! Got to catch them all It's you and me ♪

24
00:01:18.466 --> 00:01:21.500
♪ Pokémon! I know it's my destiny ♪

25
00:01:21.566 --> 00:01:24.899
♪ Pokémon! Yeah, you're my best friend ♪

26
00:01:24.966 --> 00:01:27.333
♪ In a world we must defend ♪

27
00:01:27.399 --> 00:01:29.833
♪ Pokémon! Got to catch them all ♪

28
00:01:29.899 --> 00:01:32.899
♪ Got to catch them all! Pokémon ♪

29
00:01:45.866 --> 00:01:47.933
Look! Over there!

30
00:01:51.533 --> 00:01:53.733
- Snorlax!
- Pika! Pika!

31
00:01:53.800 --> 00:01:56.433
Never seen one before!

32
00:01:56.500 --> 00:01:58.199
Hmm.

33
00:01:59.300 --> 00:02:01.666
Snorlax, the Sleeping Pokémon.

34
00:02:01.733 --> 00:02:04.466
After eating its fill, Snorlax is too sleepy to move.

35
00:02:04.533 --> 00:02:06.666
Small children sometimes play on its belly.

36
00:02:06.733 --> 00:02:10.433
I'm certain that the sound you heard was Snorlax's snoring.

37
00:02:10.500 --> 00:02:13.266
But why is it sleeping right in the center of town?

38
00:02:13.333 --> 00:02:16.766
This town and Snorlax have always had a symbiotic relationship.

39
00:02:16.833 --> 00:02:18.100
Symbiotic?

40
00:02:18.166 --> 00:02:20.166
She means they help each other out!

41
00:02:20.233 --> 00:02:23.266
Right! Every year about this time,

42
00:02:23.333 --> 00:02:27.000
Snorlax comes down from the mountaintop to eat up all the crop roots

43
00:02:27.066 --> 00:02:29.533
that are left over after we've finished our harvest.

44
00:02:29.600 --> 00:02:31.633
Wait. Isn't that a bad thing?

45
00:02:31.700 --> 00:02:33.166
Not at all!

46
00:02:33.233 --> 00:02:36.666
In fact, as Snorlax digs up the roots, it ploughs the fields,

47
00:02:36.733 --> 00:02:39.299
which gives us a good harvest the next year.

48
00:02:39.366 --> 00:02:40.666
Wow!

49
00:02:40.733 --> 00:02:43.733
Then, when Snorlax is almost finished eating,

50
00:02:43.799 --> 00:02:46.333
we have a harvest festival as a way of showing Snorlax

51
00:02:46.400 --> 00:02:48.166
our gratitude for its help.

52
00:02:48.233 --> 00:02:53.133
At the close of the festival, the Lord of Shabonneau Castle plays the Poké Flute

53
00:02:53.200 --> 00:02:55.600
while Snorlax finishes up the town's offerings

54
00:02:55.666 --> 00:02:59.233
and then it dances all the way back up to its mountaintop home.

55
00:02:59.299 --> 00:03:02.233
Does that mean the festival hasn't happened yet?

56
00:03:02.299 --> 00:03:03.733
- You see--
- Wake up!

57
00:03:03.799 --> 00:03:06.166
Come on, wake up!

58
00:03:06.233 --> 00:03:09.166
We want to see you dance, so please wake up, Snorlax!

59
00:03:09.233 --> 00:03:12.066
The town is all ready for the festival to begin,

60
00:03:12.133 --> 00:03:14.666
but the way things are there's no way we'll be able to.

61
00:03:14.733 --> 00:03:18.100
We have a big problem that's keeping Snorlax from waking up!

62
00:03:18.166 --> 00:03:19.666
What's the big problem?

63
00:03:19.733 --> 00:03:23.233
The Lord of Shabonneau Castle, who plays the flute to wake Snorlax,

64
00:03:23.299 --> 00:03:25.633
flatly refuses to come to this year's festival!

65
00:03:25.700 --> 00:03:29.066
- Oh!

66
00:03:31.866 --> 00:03:35.133
- Ow! Stop!
- It feels like my ears are going to burst!

67
00:03:35.200 --> 00:03:39.466
Heh-heh-heh! I'd say this is my cue to step in and help!

68
00:03:39.533 --> 00:03:42.666
Which means the future is now, thanks to science!

69
00:03:42.733 --> 00:03:44.366
Huh?

70
00:03:44.433 --> 00:03:48.833
I have the perfect device for this situation! Clemontic Gear on!

71
00:03:48.899 --> 00:03:52.733
I invented it to help Bonnie get out of bed, because she takes forever!

72
00:03:52.799 --> 00:03:54.899
It's the Bonnie Out of Bed-omatic!

73
00:03:54.966 --> 00:03:57.899
- What?
- That thing's going to wake up Snorlax?

74
00:03:57.966 --> 00:04:02.066
Indeed! Cranking the volume as far as it will go.

75
00:04:02.133 --> 00:04:06.233
Now make sure your ears are all covered and go!

76
00:04:07.733 --> 00:04:11.100
Morning, ring, ring, ring!

77
00:04:11.166 --> 00:04:13.600
Ring, ring, ring!

78
00:04:13.666 --> 00:04:15.700
Ring, ring, ring.

79
00:04:15.766 --> 00:04:18.700
Stop! Quiet, both of you!

80
00:04:18.766 --> 00:04:21.966
- Ring! Ring! Ring...
- Something's clearly wrong!

81
00:04:24.466 --> 00:04:26.133
I don't think it worked.

82
00:04:26.200 --> 00:04:30.233
But I'm sure that explosion was loud enough to wake Snorlax up!

83
00:04:33.700 --> 00:04:36.866
- I don't think so.
- Just get up already!

84
00:04:38.400 --> 00:04:41.400
What do you think's going to happen if Snorlax doesn't wake up?

85
00:04:41.466 --> 00:04:44.300
Nobody will get any sleep and we'll all be a wreck!

86
00:04:44.366 --> 00:04:47.666
Maybe if Nurse Joy took Snorlax in at the Pokémon Center.

87
00:04:47.733 --> 00:04:50.500
Perhaps. Maybe. Perhaps we could ask Officer Jenny.

88
00:04:50.566 --> 00:04:54.233
People are having a hard time, but I feel bad for Snorlax, too.

89
00:04:54.300 --> 00:04:57.633
We've got to help Snorlax out before it gets in more trouble.

90
00:04:57.700 --> 00:05:01.099
- I can't leave it like this.
- Yeah!

91
00:05:01.166 --> 00:05:03.266
It seems the only way it'll wake it up is

92
00:05:03.333 --> 00:05:06.466
if the Lord of Shabonneau Castle plays the Poké Flute.

93
00:05:06.533 --> 00:05:10.099
So why don't we just ask the Lord of Shabonneau Castle to come help us out?

94
00:05:10.166 --> 00:05:14.033
The townspeople have asked Lord Shabonneau several times,

95
00:05:14.099 --> 00:05:17.099
but he always seems to have an excuse for why he can't.

96
00:05:17.166 --> 00:05:20.966
- Then I'll go to Shabonneau Castle myself!
- Huh? You will?

97
00:05:21.033 --> 00:05:23.833
He'll say yes! If I tell him what's going on,

98
00:05:23.900 --> 00:05:26.000
I'm sure he'll play the flute for Snorlax!

99
00:05:26.066 --> 00:05:27.099
- Yes!
- Ash's right!

100
00:05:27.166 --> 00:05:29.333
- Pika! Pikachu!
- Huh?

101
00:05:31.666 --> 00:05:34.900
- Hello?
- Pika!

102
00:05:40.200 --> 00:05:44.599
Hello there. How can I help you young people out on this fine afternoon?

103
00:05:44.666 --> 00:05:46.666
We'd like to talk to Lord Shabonneau

104
00:05:46.733 --> 00:05:49.333
for all the people who live down in Camphrier Town.

105
00:05:49.400 --> 00:05:53.066
Well, you certainly have traveled a long way, so please, come in!

106
00:05:55.133 --> 00:05:58.566
Presenting the master of this castle, Lord Shabonneau.

107
00:05:58.633 --> 00:06:00.700
Shabonneau, bonne, bonne!

108
00:06:00.766 --> 00:06:03.066
So tell me, what brings you to my castle home?

109
00:06:03.133 --> 00:06:05.599
We need your help! Please play the flute

110
00:06:05.666 --> 00:06:08.500
at this year's harvest festival, like you've always done!

111
00:06:08.566 --> 00:06:11.666
- That is not up for discussion!
- Huh?

112
00:06:11.733 --> 00:06:13.733
- Please, sir, come back!
- Pika!

113
00:06:13.800 --> 00:06:16.933
Snorlax is asleep in the center of town and won't wake up!

114
00:06:17.000 --> 00:06:19.633
- We need you to play the Poké Flute!
- Oh, pretty please!

115
00:06:19.700 --> 00:06:25.366
Hmm. I would if I could, but no can do! I'm allergic to the flute now!

116
00:06:25.433 --> 00:06:29.633
So when I play, I then break out in hives!

117
00:06:29.700 --> 00:06:33.000
So, if you can't play, then just lend us your flute!

118
00:06:33.066 --> 00:06:35.666
I've also developed such an acute fear of flutes

119
00:06:35.733 --> 00:06:39.500
that just looking at it scared me, so I'm afraid I threw it away!

120
00:06:39.566 --> 00:06:41.733
-Threw it away?

121
00:06:41.799 --> 00:06:44.799
Lord Shabonneau, I understand you're saying all of this

122
00:06:44.866 --> 00:06:46.400
to protect your family name,

123
00:06:46.466 --> 00:06:49.933
but I'm certain you'll regret lying to these children later,

124
00:06:50.000 --> 00:06:52.000
so perhaps you should just tell the truth.

125
00:06:52.066 --> 00:06:56.400
What to do? Oh, dear! All right, here's the truth.

126
00:06:56.466 --> 00:07:00.299
The Poké Flute was in my castle at one time, not now.

127
00:07:00.366 --> 00:07:02.333
But what happened to it?

128
00:07:02.400 --> 00:07:05.333
- Did somebody break it?
- No, nothing like that!

129
00:07:05.400 --> 00:07:07.733
- Ah, that's good.
- Ah! So, what happened?

130
00:07:07.799 --> 00:07:11.099
- I'm afraid she just grabbed it.
- Huh?

131
00:07:11.166 --> 00:07:13.333
Princess Allie from Parfum Palace

132
00:07:13.400 --> 00:07:16.000
located in the next town visited my castle.

133
00:07:16.066 --> 00:07:19.766
She exclaimed, "Oh, ho, ho! This Poké Flute is so pretty!"

134
00:07:19.833 --> 00:07:21.500
And took it home with her.

135
00:07:21.566 --> 00:07:24.099
Wait! You just allowed the princess to take it?

136
00:07:24.166 --> 00:07:26.633
You see, once Princess Allie makes up her mind,

137
00:07:26.700 --> 00:07:28.766
it's impossible to get her to change it.

138
00:07:28.833 --> 00:07:31.133
- He's right!
- And you're okay with that?

139
00:07:31.200 --> 00:07:33.166
It's a family heirloom, isn't it?

140
00:07:33.233 --> 00:07:34.500
Sadly, it is.

141
00:07:34.566 --> 00:07:38.966
Princess Allie's father's been kind to me, so I couldn't put my foot down.

142
00:07:39.033 --> 00:07:41.500
Well, you can count on me to get it back from her!

143
00:07:41.566 --> 00:07:44.766
No doubt! Then you'll be able to play it at the festival!

144
00:07:44.833 --> 00:07:48.666
Splendid! I'd be delighted to perform at the Harvest Festival!

145
00:07:48.733 --> 00:07:50.566
- Okay, let's go!
- Right!

146
00:07:50.633 --> 00:07:53.166
Why don't we wait for them in Camphrier Town?

147
00:07:53.233 --> 00:07:54.933
As you wish.

148
00:07:55.000 --> 00:07:57.099
Did you get a load of that crazy scene?

149
00:07:57.166 --> 00:08:01.233
It sounds to me like that Poké Flute has control over Snorlax.

150
00:08:01.299 --> 00:08:03.266
If that flute can control Snorlax,

151
00:08:03.333 --> 00:08:05.633
then catching Pikachu will be a piece of cake!

152
00:08:05.700 --> 00:08:07.700
Think of it! We could build the Boss

153
00:08:07.766 --> 00:08:09.933
a bodacious, bombastic band of Snorlax!

154
00:08:10.000 --> 00:08:13.700
If we do that, Team Rocket will, dare I say, rule the world!

155
00:08:13.766 --> 00:08:16.900
And there's a promotion for us in there somewhere!

156
00:08:16.966 --> 00:08:20.566
- No time to waste!
- Let's make haste!

157
00:08:26.066 --> 00:08:29.200
I'd say this hedge is part of Parfum Palace.

158
00:08:30.266 --> 00:08:31.933
Bonnie, what are you doing?

159
00:08:32.000 --> 00:08:35.400
I think we can sneak in right through here!

160
00:08:39.133 --> 00:08:41.433
Wow!

161
00:08:41.500 --> 00:08:42.866
What a giant garden!

162
00:08:42.933 --> 00:08:44.933
I wouldn't want to mow the lawn.

163
00:08:48.833 --> 00:08:50.333
Who's that Pokémon?

164
00:08:50.400 --> 00:08:52.400
You know that one. It's a Furfrou.

165
00:08:52.466 --> 00:08:55.600
Oh. That's a Furfrou too?

166
00:08:55.666 --> 00:08:57.966
Furfrou, stop at once!

167
00:09:04.800 --> 00:09:08.466
Furfrou dear, you shouldn't be playing with all this trash.

168
00:09:08.533 --> 00:09:12.033
- It'll give you a tummy ache.
- Hey! You calling us trash?

169
00:09:12.100 --> 00:09:14.300
Uh, might you be Princess Allie?

170
00:09:14.366 --> 00:09:19.699
Hm. Indeed, I am Princess Allie.

171
00:09:19.766 --> 00:09:21.400
Parfum Palace is my home!

172
00:09:21.466 --> 00:09:22.966
So lovely!

173
00:09:23.033 --> 00:09:25.333
- Wow, you're a real princess?
- Na-na!

174
00:09:25.400 --> 00:09:28.166
Getting the flute back might not be so easy.

175
00:09:28.233 --> 00:09:31.766
Please, Princess Allie! Give us the Poké Flute back all right.

176
00:09:31.833 --> 00:09:34.466
- Not going to happen.
- But why not?

177
00:09:34.533 --> 00:09:36.000
Because my things are my things

178
00:09:36.066 --> 00:09:38.600
and things that were given to me are my things as well,

179
00:09:38.666 --> 00:09:41.400
so the Poké Flute is one of my things and it's all mine!

180
00:09:42.966 --> 00:09:45.766
- She's weird.
- She's awful and she's selfish, too!

181
00:09:45.833 --> 00:09:49.100
The town won't be able to have the Harvest Festival without the flute!

182
00:09:49.166 --> 00:09:52.433
And Snorlax is snoring so loudly that the townspeople can't get any sleep!

183
00:09:52.500 --> 00:09:56.833
If so they should just go to their seaside villas and take a little nappy-poo.

184
00:09:59.000 --> 00:10:02.400
At this rate, the townspeople are going to end up hating Snorlax!

185
00:10:02.466 --> 00:10:04.933
- I can't let that happen!
- Pika! Pika!

186
00:10:05.000 --> 00:10:07.933
- Oh?
- Pika?

187
00:10:08.000 --> 00:10:10.566
- Hm.
- Pika?

188
00:10:10.633 --> 00:10:13.166
Would this Pikachu belong to you?

189
00:10:13.233 --> 00:10:14.733
Yeah! My partner!

190
00:10:14.800 --> 00:10:18.066
Every Pikachu has different size cheeks than other Pikachu.

191
00:10:18.133 --> 00:10:20.300
Yours has perfectly-sized cheeks

192
00:10:20.366 --> 00:10:23.366
and the roundness and redness are just right. Splendid!

193
00:10:23.433 --> 00:10:25.566
Pika!

194
00:10:25.633 --> 00:10:28.900
Such a splendid and rare Pikachu is unworthy of you,

195
00:10:28.966 --> 00:10:33.066
so I'll graciously accept it and treasure it like an heirloom.

196
00:10:33.133 --> 00:10:38.500
Ah! No way! Pikachu's my buddy and that's the end of that!

197
00:10:38.566 --> 00:10:42.066
- Hm! Bring them out.
- Ma'am!

198
00:10:46.800 --> 00:10:50.333
What if I give all of these treasures for Pikachu?

199
00:10:50.400 --> 00:10:52.933
- That's crazy!
- You're out of your mind!

200
00:10:54.833 --> 00:11:01.233
Hm. Huh! Hm! If I recall, you want the Poké Flute, correct?

201
00:11:01.300 --> 00:11:02.933
Yeah! Will you give it back?

202
00:11:03.000 --> 00:11:06.833
Let's have a battle, Furfrou versus Pikachu.

203
00:11:06.900 --> 00:11:10.166
I suggest that we bet the Poké Flute and Pikachu!

204
00:11:10.233 --> 00:11:12.900
- No way!
- How could you do such an awful thing?

205
00:11:12.966 --> 00:11:15.266
- Ew!
- We can forget it.

206
00:11:15.333 --> 00:11:18.100
But I'm warning you that this is your one and only chance

207
00:11:18.166 --> 00:11:19.900
to get your hands on that flute.

208
00:11:19.966 --> 00:11:22.066
- Oh, man.
- Pika!

209
00:11:22.133 --> 00:11:24.600
- Huh?
- Huh! Pika! Pi!

210
00:11:24.666 --> 00:11:26.900
Pikachu! You'll go through with it?

211
00:11:26.966 --> 00:11:28.566
Pikachu!

212
00:11:28.633 --> 00:11:31.300
Hm.

213
00:11:31.366 --> 00:11:34.300
It's a deal! You're on!

214
00:11:34.366 --> 00:11:35.833
Excellent.

215
00:11:35.900 --> 00:11:38.300
Who's that Pokémon?

216
00:11:42.900 --> 00:11:45.199
It's Snorlax!

217
00:11:50.600 --> 00:11:53.900
All right, if I win, you're going to return that Poké Flute!

218
00:11:53.966 --> 00:11:56.400
Enough talk, let us began.

219
00:11:56.466 --> 00:11:59.199
Pikachu versus Furfrou in a one-on-one battle!

220
00:11:59.266 --> 00:12:02.966
The battle will be over when either Pokémon is unable to continue, agreed?

221
00:12:03.033 --> 00:12:05.199
- Okay!
- That's fine with me.

222
00:12:05.266 --> 00:12:07.933
All right, battle begin!

223
00:12:10.633 --> 00:12:13.800
- Okay, Pikachu, use Quick Attack!
- Pika!

224
00:12:13.866 --> 00:12:18.400
This should be easy, Furfrou!

225
00:12:18.466 --> 00:12:22.766
- Furfrou!
- Pik!

226
00:12:24.066 --> 00:12:26.733
Pikachu... Pika?

227
00:12:29.033 --> 00:12:32.033
- Look out! Behind you!
- Pika!

228
00:12:32.100 --> 00:12:36.500
- Pikachu, Iron Tail, let's go!
- And now, Furfrou, use Bite!

229
00:12:36.566 --> 00:12:40.966
Pikachu!

230
00:12:42.233 --> 00:12:44.400
- Pikachu, are you okay?
- Pikachu!

231
00:12:44.466 --> 00:12:47.599
Nice, but that's about as far as you'll get.

232
00:12:47.666 --> 00:12:51.199
Let us scatter the rose's glorious bloom with style and grace!

233
00:12:51.266 --> 00:12:55.633
Furfrou, use Charge Beam!

234
00:12:55.699 --> 00:13:02.466
- Pikachu, counter it, with Electro Ball!
- Pika! Pika! Pikachu!

235
00:13:05.099 --> 00:13:09.199
- Now use Thunderbolt!
- Pikachu!

236
00:13:13.900 --> 00:13:17.000
No! How dare you do that to my Furfrou?

237
00:13:17.066 --> 00:13:19.033
-Furfrou's got a new hairdo!

238
00:13:19.099 --> 00:13:21.066
Great job, Pikachu!

239
00:13:21.133 --> 00:13:23.433
Take Furfrou to the groomer right away!

240
00:13:23.500 --> 00:13:26.333
- As you wish, ma'am.
- Furfrou...

241
00:13:26.400 --> 00:13:28.500
Hold on! What about our battle?

242
00:13:28.566 --> 00:13:31.266
Princess Allie! Are you forfeiting?

243
00:13:31.333 --> 00:13:35.433
It can't be helped! My Furfrou can't battle looking so atrocious!

244
00:13:35.500 --> 00:13:38.500
So that would mean a forfeit and Pikachu's the winner!

245
00:13:38.566 --> 00:13:42.033
- All right! We did it, buddy!
- Pikachu!

246
00:13:42.099 --> 00:13:45.133
Now, it's time for you to give Lord Shabonneau's Poké Flute back!

247
00:13:45.199 --> 00:13:47.866
I will not return anything, since I lost.

248
00:13:47.933 --> 00:13:49.933
-Pika!

249
00:13:50.000 --> 00:13:53.366
- That wasn't the deal we made!
- Pika!

250
00:13:53.433 --> 00:13:56.433
Huh! If you were listening, the only thing I said was that

251
00:13:56.500 --> 00:14:00.466
we would be betting the Poké Flute and Pikachu in our battle and nothing more!

252
00:14:00.533 --> 00:14:03.300
After I beat you, I was going to give you the poke flute.

253
00:14:03.366 --> 00:14:05.199
but since you're the winner, I insist

254
00:14:05.266 --> 00:14:08.566
that you hand over Pikachu to me.

255
00:14:08.633 --> 00:14:11.099
What kind of bet is that? -Really!

256
00:14:11.166 --> 00:14:14.333
- It makes no sense!
- Pika, pika!

257
00:14:14.400 --> 00:14:16.866
Ha! Well, I'm the princess of this palace

258
00:14:16.933 --> 00:14:20.066
and that means I make all the rules! Something wrong?

259
00:14:20.133 --> 00:14:23.933
Your unscientific selfishness might be tolerated at your palace,

260
00:14:24.000 --> 00:14:26.000
but not out in the real world!

261
00:14:26.066 --> 00:14:29.566
- We refuse your ridiculous demands!
- Uh...

262
00:14:29.633 --> 00:14:34.199
Ash battled against you even if it meant putting his precious partner on the line!

263
00:14:34.266 --> 00:14:38.166
Of course he trusted that you'd give up the flute if he won!

264
00:14:38.233 --> 00:14:41.066
If you insist on acting so selfishly,

265
00:14:41.133 --> 00:14:44.166
I'm afraid you're not going to have any friends left! -Huh?

266
00:14:44.233 --> 00:14:46.766
-I think you're being a little too harsh.

267
00:14:46.833 --> 00:14:48.766
You didn't have to yell at her like that.

268
00:14:48.833 --> 00:14:51.833
But somebody needed to tell her the truth!

269
00:14:51.900 --> 00:14:56.000
It's all right. You scolded me with much sincerity.

270
00:14:56.066 --> 00:14:59.199
That means you must care about me a great deal, don't you?

271
00:14:59.266 --> 00:15:02.066
- I what?
- I truly understand.

272
00:15:02.133 --> 00:15:03.633
There's no need for words.

273
00:15:03.699 --> 00:15:08.099
- You don't understand!
- I don't? Hm!

274
00:15:08.166 --> 00:15:11.699
Hm. I suppose you can have the Poké Flute back.

275
00:15:11.766 --> 00:15:14.233
- Huh.
- Under one condition!

276
00:15:14.300 --> 00:15:16.166
I'm not giving you Pikachu!

277
00:15:16.233 --> 00:15:20.466
In exchange for the Poké Flute, I insist that you leave this one with me.

278
00:15:20.533 --> 00:15:23.666
Ah! You want me to stay?

279
00:15:23.733 --> 00:15:25.699
Huh?

280
00:15:27.099 --> 00:15:29.000
- Do you think so?
- Yeah.

281
00:15:29.066 --> 00:15:30.933
You can have my brother if you want him!

282
00:15:31.000 --> 00:15:33.266
Bonnie, how could you tell her that?

283
00:15:33.333 --> 00:15:35.800
All right. It's settled.

284
00:15:35.866 --> 00:15:37.133
Ma'am.

285
00:15:38.633 --> 00:15:41.766
Now! Please give them the Poké Flute.

286
00:15:46.199 --> 00:15:49.866
- Here. It's yours.
- You have your precious Poké Flute now.

287
00:15:49.933 --> 00:15:51.133
Thank you!

288
00:15:51.199 --> 00:15:53.866
We got to go. Have a good time, big brother!

289
00:15:53.933 --> 00:15:55.866
But you guys!

290
00:15:55.933 --> 00:15:58.633
After we wake up Snorlax, we'll come back.

291
00:15:58.699 --> 00:16:00.266
Just hang in there for a while.

292
00:16:00.333 --> 00:16:04.433
- But, Ash, help me!
- Don't worry! It'll be fine.

293
00:16:06.333 --> 00:16:09.333
Um, are you really sure about this?

294
00:16:10.833 --> 00:16:12.833
Everything will be fine, Clemont!

295
00:16:12.900 --> 00:16:14.733
Congratulations, Princess!

296
00:16:14.800 --> 00:16:17.266
Take good care of my brother, okay?

297
00:16:17.333 --> 00:16:21.500
Guys, please don't go! Don't leave me!

298
00:16:28.566 --> 00:16:30.733
Hm.

299
00:16:30.800 --> 00:16:32.533
- Lord Shabonneau!
- Huh?

300
00:16:33.599 --> 00:16:35.900
- They're back!

301
00:16:35.966 --> 00:16:39.500
It's true! And with the Poké Flute!

302
00:16:39.566 --> 00:16:43.966
We got it back, just like we promised! Now, please play it!

303
00:16:44.033 --> 00:16:45.699
Yes!

304
00:16:48.199 --> 00:16:51.866
- My flute! What's going on?
- Huh?

305
00:16:51.933 --> 00:16:53.666
- Oh!
- Lord Shabonneau!

306
00:16:53.733 --> 00:16:55.666
Pika!

307
00:16:57.800 --> 00:16:59.733
Huh?

308
00:16:59.800 --> 00:17:01.900
I should have known it was you!

309
00:17:01.966 --> 00:17:04.266
Prepare for trouble, you don't know much!

310
00:17:04.333 --> 00:17:06.300
And make it double, you're so out of touch!

311
00:17:06.366 --> 00:17:08.800
To protect the world from devastation!

312
00:17:08.866 --> 00:17:11.466
To unite all people within our nation!

313
00:17:11.533 --> 00:17:14.666
To denounce the evils of a twerp with a flute!

314
00:17:14.733 --> 00:17:18.033
We extend our reach, then the problem is moot!

315
00:17:18.099 --> 00:17:20.700
- Jessie!
- And James!

316
00:17:20.766 --> 00:17:23.666
Team Rocket blasts off at the speed of light!

317
00:17:23.733 --> 00:17:26.533
Surrender now or prepare for a musical fight!

318
00:17:26.599 --> 00:17:29.733
- Meowth, that's right!
- Wobbuffet!

319
00:17:31.100 --> 00:17:32.500
Perfecto.

320
00:17:32.566 --> 00:17:35.033
The flute that controls Snorlax controls the world!

321
00:17:35.100 --> 00:17:37.033
Yeah and that's the name of that tune!

322
00:17:37.100 --> 00:17:39.533
I'm the only one who can play that flute!

323
00:17:39.600 --> 00:17:41.066
We'll see about that.

324
00:17:41.133 --> 00:17:43.300
We'll give it a test run and play a few riffs!

325
00:17:43.366 --> 00:17:45.366
Oh, no! Don't do it!

326
00:17:45.433 --> 00:17:48.266
Your Highness doth protest too much, methinks.

327
00:17:48.333 --> 00:17:50.300
Play us a tune, maestro!

328
00:17:50.366 --> 00:17:52.666
See sharp or be flat!

329
00:17:52.733 --> 00:17:54.866
My ears!

330
00:17:54.933 --> 00:17:57.766
- Huh?
- I think you need to take lessons.

331
00:17:57.833 --> 00:18:00.966
For the next five hundred years!

332
00:18:01.033 --> 00:18:04.466
I tried to tell you, nobody can play it but me.

333
00:18:07.166 --> 00:18:09.633
- Whoa!
- Snorlax woke up!

334
00:18:09.700 --> 00:18:13.433
And that awful noise put Snorlax in a bad mood!

335
00:18:13.500 --> 00:18:16.300
Snorlax!

336
00:18:16.366 --> 00:18:20.366
Hm. You see that? Hats off, folks, I'm a genius!

337
00:18:20.433 --> 00:18:22.300
All right, Snorlax, obey me!

338
00:18:31.266 --> 00:18:34.399
- I blew it!
- We're blasting off again!

339
00:18:34.466 --> 00:18:36.700
Wobbuffet!

340
00:18:38.766 --> 00:18:41.300
Lord Shabonneau!

341
00:18:41.366 --> 00:18:43.666
- Your flute!
- Thanks! I'll play!

342
00:18:50.633 --> 00:18:52.633
Look. Here comes Snorlax!

343
00:18:58.533 --> 00:19:00.899
Wow! Look at Snorlax go!

344
00:19:00.966 --> 00:19:02.966
Thanks so much for all your help again this year!

345
00:19:03.033 --> 00:19:04.533
Yay! Snorlax, go!

346
00:19:08.399 --> 00:19:10.233
What a relief.

347
00:19:13.233 --> 00:19:16.733
Bye, Snorlax!

348
00:19:17.800 --> 00:19:19.966
Everything worked out just fine.

349
00:19:20.033 --> 00:19:22.433
- Isn't it great, buddy?
- Pikachu!

350
00:19:22.500 --> 00:19:25.399
The Poké Flute has been returned to its rightful owners

351
00:19:25.466 --> 00:19:28.600
and the bond between Snorlax and the townspeople is even stronger,

352
00:19:28.666 --> 00:19:31.800
thanks to our heroes, Ash, Pikachu, Serena, and Bonnie.

353
00:19:31.866 --> 00:19:34.966
- Um, aren't we forgetting something?
- Huh?

354
00:19:35.033 --> 00:19:37.466
Ah! Clemont!

355
00:19:37.533 --> 00:19:39.633
Oh!

356
00:19:39.700 --> 00:19:45.366
Bonnie! You guys!

357
00:19:45.433 --> 00:19:46.766
Clemont?

358
00:19:46.833 --> 00:19:50.833
- It was horrible.
- What happened to all your clothes?

359
00:19:50.899 --> 00:19:54.933
- Oh, I can't look!!
- So how did you get out?

360
00:19:55.000 --> 00:19:58.800
- Ah, it's all thanks to science!
- Huh?

361
00:19:58.866 --> 00:20:02.866
Clemont! Clemont!

362
00:20:02.933 --> 00:20:06.600
Everything is all prepared for the fireworks festival!

363
00:20:06.666 --> 00:20:09.800
Clemont? Are you listening?

364
00:20:09.866 --> 00:20:13.899
Thank you for your concern. Now, if you'll excuse me, I'll be on my way.

365
00:20:13.966 --> 00:20:18.666
What is this? Clemont tricked me!

366
00:20:18.733 --> 00:20:20.800
And I refuse to be tricked!

367
00:20:29.899 --> 00:20:33.833
- Look, fireworks!
- Beautiful!

368
00:20:33.899 --> 00:20:38.233
As I was saying, the Poké Flute was returned to its royal, rightful owner

369
00:20:38.300 --> 00:20:41.733
and the bond between Snorlax and the townspeople is intact

370
00:20:41.800 --> 00:20:45.433
and stronger than ever as the journey continues!
